# Dot pixel effects

Use this when the user asks for 도트, 픽셀, 도트 그래픽, 기술 이펙트, sprite pixels, or a reference clip for move VFX.

## Request that produced this look

- Keep the feel of dot / pixel skill effects. Do not replace them with smooth vectors, soft glows, or anti-aliased strokes.
- Each effect pixel is the same size as each character sprite pixel. Bigger shapes mean more pixels, not larger pixels.
- Rebuild the effect from scratch when the reference changes. Do not stack a new layer on the old renderer.
- Fix awkward character motion in the same pass: feet on the shadow, no squash or rotation of the sprite, attack sheets that finish their lunge.
- Keywords to keep: 도트, 1픽셀, 스프라이트 픽셀, 픽셀 그리드, nearest-neighbor, 화염방사, 10만볼트, 파도타기, 에너지볼, tongue, branch, foam, leaf, outline, core.

## Rules

- One effect cell is `ArenaFX.PIXEL` world units, blitted with `imageSmoothingEnabled = false` from a 1×1 source pixel.
- Battle PIXEL is 1.43. The motion studio must call `ArenaFX.setPixel(spriteScale)` before drawing, so studio pixels match the enlarged sprite.
- Snap sprites and shadows to that same grid. `spritePose` may shift by whole pixels only. No `rotate`, non-uniform scale, or sub-pixel squash on the character.
- Draw effects as authored cells: 4-color palette per element (outline, body, mid, core), hard edges, animation stepped at about 12–18 Hz.
- Reference clip on `main`: `YTDown.com_YouTube_Media_J_JhLHfqZXY_Pokemon-Arena-2D-by-Big-Kid-Nation-Fan-Game-95-real-gameplay_003_480p.mp4` (Big Kid Nation Pokémon Arena 2D, about 2:02, 854×480). Read that file before changing silhouettes.
- Flamethrower, traced from the reference clip around 34–40s: a connected chain of round lobes with a small hot core, not a bullseye. It starts narrow at the mouth, widens into a cloud, and throws a few detached bulbs. A 1px dark edge and a faint orange fringe sit on the outside.
- Thunderbolt: a jagged bolt of the same pixels, white core, short branches, spark ring on the body.
- Surf and cannon jets: water lobes and a thick jet (white core, cyan, dark edge), not a hairline. Steam on a fire impact is a column of light pixels.
- Energy Ball: one filled green lobe with small leaf pixels around it.
- Bigger shapes mean more 1×1 cells. Do not scale a pixel up, blur it, or draw it with arcs.
- Flat oval shadow under the feet. No sprite rotation or squash. Walk steps follow distance. A dodge plays the Attack sheet through the lunge.
- Do not add per-frame random particle clouds on top of these effects. Damage, cooldowns, and hitboxes stay as they are.
